I'm noting that since I'm using the literal --wall sphere case command, and a sphere has no sharp edges at the default 45-degree feature angle, running surfaceFeatureEdges wouldn't actually split it into indexed patches.

For the box, though, each face is already its own named solid before the split, and since the faces are flat with no internal feature edges, surfaceFeatureEdges shouldn't subdivide them further—but it may still append an index suffix to each name simply due to how the tool processes solids, regardless of whether a split occurs.

